schema: source-system
object:
  title: KOI-net (BlockScience / Metagov / RMIT)
  type: repo
  steward: BlockScience, with Metagov and RMIT
  what_it_curates: >-
    The KOI-net protocol and its MIT-licensed Python implementation
    (`koi-net` on GitHub) — network protocol for federating knowledge across
    organizational boundaries via RIDs and sensor/processor/coordinator node
    roles. The article notes the Regen Toolkit already wires a `regen-koi`
    integration and treats its own repo layout as "sensor-friendly today."
  why_it_matters: >-
    The most structured federation protocol option cited in the article, and
    directly relevant since the Toolkit already has a regen-koi integration
    path.
  url: 'https://github.com/BlockScience/koi-net'
  use_type: protocol/reference implementation to evaluate for future federation
  reuse_conditions: MIT-licensed (per the article)
  return_path: 'GitHub issues/PRs on BlockScience/koi-net — not explicitly confirmed as a maintained contribution channel here'
  currentness: 'public beta since May 2025; v2.0.7 as of May 2026 per the article'
  update_rhythm: actively maintained (per the article)
  extraction_status: partial — only the framing given in this article has been captured, not the protocol docs themselves
  toolkit_route: layer-10-infrastructure-and-substrate
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/federation-portability.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
